 Well, how's this for a VERY frustrating way to go :

 Em the Wizard blinked and looked at his surroundings. This had to be
the Astral Plane, that magical place where his long and tedious quest
would come to an end. He heard a voice in his head telling him he had
done well so far, and an Angel appeared before him and smiled friendly
at him.
 Opening the first door, Em found himself jumped by hordes of Priests of
Moloch aided by a few not-so-friendly Angels. But aided by his trusty
Vorpal Blade he advanced leaving many beheaded priests in his trail.
 Suddenly, a demon of such an uglyness that Em winced, appeared before
him. "I am death, and you are as good as dead", croaked the hideous
creature.  Em frowned and then slew Death with one mighty blow from his
sword.  
 Dispatching some more priests, Em finally found an Altar.  But alas, it
was a Lawful altar. Not to be outdone so easily, Em reached in his
magical bag of Holding and got out his Helm of Opposite Alignment.
 A few moments later, Em the now-lawful-wizard held up the Amulet of
Yendor and sacrificed it.

